From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:23:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 28/38] Scroll to views with ScrollViewReader on Linux

A scroll view keeps where its targets are: the children of lazy stacks
and the rows of lists, by the identifier of their ForEach element or
their id. ScrollViewProxy.scrollTo scrolls the first scroll view in the
reader that has the target, its anchor at the same point of the view or
just enough to show it, animated inside withAnimation; a target not laid
out yet is scrolled to once it is. An optional identifier stands for its
value.
